## Evidence

Planning uses project `llmist`, target-qualified agent `llmist-plan`, repository
`zbigniewsobiecki/llmist`, base `dev`. The source identities and workflow blobs above
are verified locally and dev's head is confirmed through GitHub MCP. The parent
amendment is merged via PR #691. Runner, environment and secret facts are supplied
Root/operator observations, not independent live settings reads. Available tools
do not expose those inventories. Both new prerequisites remain pending.

### Implementation — 2026-11-16

Project `llmist`, target-qualified agent `llmist-implement`, repository
`zbigniewsobiecki/llmist`, base `dev`. Checkout, `origin/dev` and GitHub MCP's live
dev head all match `980e47fd294edd5df13f9c29aa11fa97cdbd9816`. The three workflow
blobs match the preservation oracle above. MCP confirms base push run
[43654543235](https://github.com/zbigniewsobiecki/llmist/actions/runs/43654543235)
is successful at that head; this hosted baseline is not candidate execution proof.

**Execution choices.** The headless implementation assignment authorizes this
single-plan change, both pre-start gates, and completed-form plan/spec files at
the PR head with explicit deferrals. That supplied lifecycle rule supersedes the
planning-time requirement to wait for post-merge outcomes before renaming. No
acceptance check or merge gate is waived. The lock, implementation and lifecycle
evidence share the code commit to follow the target's stage/check/commit policy.
The fragment uses the assigned child identifier; previously landed Spec/Plan
fragments remain intact. No decision record or general guidance is added.

**M1 / readiness-all-pools — passed on supplied evidence.** The implementation
brief dated 2026-11-16 relays Root's verified pre-start gate through the coordinator:
fresh-per-job lifecycle is delivered by infrastructure
`91fde791594e9c0f67ab80142be3f1454940d70c`; toolchain exec repair
`71853c3b02501c7515ceb51313f7c81ec4d24df0` is applied in Pulumi update 33.
All three llmist units are idle-restarted onto the new mounts. As UID 1001,
executable probes pass in HOME, `/opt/hostedtoolcache` and `/tmp/runner`, where
noexec is false, on every pool. The brief explicitly confirms both pre-start
gates are satisfied. The implementer accepts that Root verification rather than
